infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Does this decision warrant an ADR?
  desc The signal — would a senior joining in two years need the WHY, and could they not infer it from the code?
  compares
    - label Warrants an ADR
      children
        - label Architectural style choice
          desc Event-driven vs request-response; monolith vs microservices
        - label Significant technology adoption
          desc Choosing a specific event store, message broker, or ORM
        - label Rejected alternative likely to return
          desc The record is what prevents re-litigating it from zero
        - label Non-obvious accepted tradeoffs
          desc Forces a future engineer cannot infer from the code
        - label Constrains future options
          desc Cannot change to X without re-implementing Y
    - label No ADR needed
      children
        - label Routine implementation choice
          desc Naming conventions, file structure within a module
        - label Framework-idiomatic pattern
          desc Using DI because the framework already uses it
        - label Obvious from code and domain
          desc PostgreSQL as the default in a Rails shop
        - label Reversible tooling choice
          desc Formatter or linter — config files are self-evident
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
